{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Starts Dating Marco"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "How's Peter?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le09ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past & Past Continuous Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was or was not happening at a particular time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class =\"strong\">Affirmative</span> form: subject + was/were + verb-ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class =\"strong\">Negative</span> form: subject + was/were + not + verb-ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Past Continuous talks about a longer \u2018background' action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Simple Past talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words <span class =\"strong\">when</span>, <span class =\"strong\">while</span> and <span class =\"strong\">as</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wasn't sleeping <span class =\"strong\">when</span> you called."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">While</span> I was reading a book, I heard a noise."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">As</span> I was waiting at the airport, I listened to music."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About the Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense (<span class =\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future.<br /> You can also use the modals <span class =\"strong\">might</span> and <span class =\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is \u2018ll."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The modals <span class =\"strong\">might</span> and <span class =\"strong\">may</span> go before the verb. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "They talk about future possibility or a chance that something will happen. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Might</span> means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%)."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "give a call"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to call someone using the telephone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll give him a call when I have some time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "weather forecast"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a description of what kind of weather is likely to happen in the future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The weather forecast for today is rain."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ice cream sandwich"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "ice cream between two cookies"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We made ice cream sandwiches yesterday."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to stumble"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to hit your foot on something when you are walking or running so that you fall or almost fall "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Marco stumbled into me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fly off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move through the air quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The cookies went flying off into the air."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to land"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to come down through the air"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The plate landed on the floor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cut"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to break the skin and make it bleed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The broken pieces cut his hand."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stitch"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a piece of thread used to sew the edges of a wound together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Marco might get a few stitches on his hand."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob11aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go on the internet. Find an English speaking radio station."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to it for 10 minutes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you listen, listen for the different tenses. Can you spot them all?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list. Write down the ones you hear."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare your list with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can listen for actions in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can listen for events in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can talk about actions and events in the past and future."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le09ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le09ob11re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le09ob11re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Did you talk to Peter?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah, he was getting ready for exams when I talked to him.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: If I get a chance, I might give him a call. <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Where are you now?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm in the Congo. The flight to Cairo is delayed for 5 hours! What will I do?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le09ob11re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Why? <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: The weather forecast for today is rain, rain and more rain! Hey, you never told me about the rest of your evening with Marco.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh right, so, we made ice cream sandwiches with the cookies Marco made. <br/>\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Right.", "id": 2, "time": "16400", "image": "engenn5le09ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: While I was taking them out of the fridge, Marco stumbled into me. Then, the sandwiches flew up into the air. The plate landed on the ground and broke. <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Wow!<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It gets better. Marco cut his hand on the broken plate.